    "body": "Adds deterministic regression coverage for the paused-send timeout introduced in #36667. Production behavior is unchanged.\n\nThe test checks that additional queued messages and send attempts preserve the original pause timer despite recent send/receive activity; expiration occurs only after TIMEOUT_INTERVAL; and draining sends bytes, clears the pause, and allows a fresh interval on the next pause.\n\nUses mock time, a null socket while paused, and ZeroSock for draining. This covers the timeout lifecycle, not real socket backpressure, partial writes, handshakes, or concurrent behavior.\n\nValidation of the submitted file contents:\n\n- macOS arm64 Debug: focused test and complete `net_tests` pass; formatting and whitespace checks pass.\n- Docker Linux arm64, `native_nowallet`: build and all 364 CTest entries pass; default functional suite reports 392 passed, 87 skipped, zero failures.\n- Local `native_asan` is running; `native_tsan` and the compile-only `win64` job are queued. Results will be added when available.\n\nAI assistance was used for implementation, review, validation, and this description. Kept as a draft pending the author's final review and remaining validation.\n",
